# Git workflow (hermes-stack)

Follow **[docs/GIT.md](../../docs/GIT.md)** as the source of truth.

## Core rule

- `develop` = everything integrating / testing
- `main` = production-ready only
- `release/*` = selected features for the next production cut

```text
feature/* ──MR──> develop ──> release/* ──MR──> main
```

## Fetch and rebase first (mandatory)

**Before implementing or promoting any change, fetch the latest remotes and rebase the current branch.** Do not start work, open an MR, or merge onto a stale base.

| When | Onto | Command |
|------|------|---------|
| Start / continue `feature/*` or `fix/*` | `origin/develop` | `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/develop` |
| Start / continue `hotfix/*` or `release/*` | `origin/main` | `git fetch origin && git rebase origin/main` |
| Promote feature → `develop` | `origin/develop` | fetch + rebase, then MR `feature/*` → `develop` |
| Promote toward production | `origin/main` | fetch + rebase `release/*` onto `origin/main`, then MR `release/*` → `main` |

```bash
git fetch origin
git rebase origin/develop   # feature/fix
git rebase origin/main      # hotfix/release
```

- Non-interactive rebase only (no `git rebase -i`).
- On conflict: resolve then `git rebase --continue`, or `--abort` and ask. Force-push only when the operator explicitly asks (`--force-with-lease`).
- **Never** merge `develop` straight into `main`.

## Merging to `main` (mandatory)

- **Always open a Pull Request / merge request into `main`.**
- **Never** `git push` new commits directly to `main`.
- **Never** merge locally to `main` and force-push.
- Production path: create/push `release/vX.Y.Z` → `gh pr create --base main` → merge **via that PR** (`[RELEASE] Release vX.Y.Z`).
- Hotfixes: `hotfix/*` → MR → `main` (then sync `develop`).

## Branches

| Branch | From | MR into |
|--------|------|---------|
| `feature/*` | `develop` | `develop` |
| `fix/*` | `develop` | `develop` |
| `hotfix/*` | `main` | `main` (+ sync `develop`) |
| `release/vX.Y.Z` | `main`, then cherry-pick ready features | `main` (**via MR only**) |

## MR title (required)

```text
[TYPE][LAYER] Imperative summary
[RELEASE] Release vX.Y.Z
```

Examples: `[FEATURE][MEMORY] Add memory manager` · `[FIX][SESSION] Fix session isolation` · `[RELEASE] Release v1.5.0`

## Must

- **Fetch + rebase first** before implementing or promoting (`origin/develop` for feature/fix, `origin/main` for hotfix/release)
- Update `docs/CHANGELOG.md` (top + timestamp) for ops/product changes
- Do not merge untested 🧪 features into `release/*` / `main`
- Do not merge `develop` straight into `main` (use `release/*` MR)
- Push only when GitHub auth is the repo owner (`7ringuy4n` for this repo)
- No VPS/remote apply without explicit permission
- Force-push / amend only when the operator explicitly asks (`--force-with-lease`)
- Do not commit `.env`, secrets, lab host/account defaults, or `scripts/temp/**` / `hermes/temp/**` drafts
